{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/529058-how-likely-would-it-be-for-a-demon-blooded-to-find-refuge-with-the-lucifuge","id":529058,"title":"How likely would it be for a Demon-Blooded to find refuge with the Lucifuge?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Hunter: The Vigil"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-05-26T11:43:52-07:00","id":529058,"title":"How likely would it be for a Demon-Blooded to find refuge with the Lucifuge?","content":"So, my question for you all is exactly what the title says.<br /> How likely would it be for the child of an Unchained Demon, a Demon-Blooded, be to find a place of refuge with the Lucifuge?<br /> <br /> I've been digging through my Hunter books since this occurred to me, because this sounds like both an awesome backstory and a good way to introduce players to the God Machine.<br /> I found a section of the fluff text in the core Hunter the Vigil book that says that the Lucifuge actually fears Angels, wouldn't having a the child of an actual fallen angel be a way to find out more information about them? Without getting their agents destroyed? Especially since they can tell when demons are lying, and see through demons Covers.<br /> <br /> And if they started recruiting Demon-Blooded that would mean they could have more than six hundred and sixty six members, which would be a boon for them. And could they cross-breed Off-spring Lucifuge children? Because I would not want to fight that, not even as a full supernatural, just because of how unpredictable that would be.<br /> <br /> I'm still thinking about what would happen if I did this as the ST in a game, what do you guys think? What would happen if the Lucifuge did open up its arms, even if it was just to recruit them as minor members.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6154-deathmonkee","name":"DeathMonkee","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6154_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"58"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-26T20:48:51-07:00","id":529571,"title":"","content":"Well first of all, you'd have to what hunter features these demon-blooded would qualify for- practical experience, risking willpower, etc? Because the default assumption is that a supernatural might not qualify for all of it.<br /> <br /> Then, you'd have to decide what benefit these demon-blooded get for joining the lucifuge- Because fluff wise, these guys wouldn't qualify for castigation. <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/391-stsword","name":"StSword","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar391_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1635"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-27T00:19:17-07:00","id":529660,"title":"","content":"I'd say they'd know he wasn't the same thing as them - but they'd be quite likely to offer refuge anyway.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-28T20:33:26-07:00","id":531647,"title":"","content":"Okay, so basic refuge is likely but if they are going to run cross-over adventure then I'm going to have to do some work on figuring out what they qualify for. Good so far then.<br /> <br /> I still don't know how likely full recruitment would be though, I guess I could say that that would be on a case-by-case basis.<br /> <br /> What about cross-breeding? Would it be possible, and would any children born be mystically viable?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6154-deathmonkee","name":"DeathMonkee","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6154_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"58"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-29T00:23:50-07:00","id":531769,"title":"","content":"Mechanically? Nothing stops a fractal or offspring from being a lucifuge, since mechanically castigation is a merit that relies on status in the lucifuge, not being a normal human. <br /> <br /> Storywise, it's not something I'd recommend, though. <br /> <br /> What I'd recommend is incorporating the two- giving the lucifuge a tendency for having supernatural merits (which is nothing a lucifuge is barred from anyway),or having castigations that reflect their gm heritage as well- like say manifesting a demon form trait with that &quot;assume demonic features&quot; castigation from C&amp;C.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/391-stsword","name":"StSword","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar391_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1635"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-29T19:19:26-07:00","id":532676,"title":"","content":"Okay, hmmmmmm.......<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <b>StSword</b> said:<br /> Mechanically? Nothing stops a fractal or offspring from being a lucifuge, since mechanically castigation is a merit that relies on status in the lucifuge, not being a normal human. </div> </div> </div>It was my understanding that a lucifuges powers, ie Castigation and the extended lifespan, came from being the child of a human and an Infernal Demon. Am I misunderstanding this?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Storywise, it's not something I'd recommend, though. </div> </div> </div>After some thought on this, I think I am in agreement as well. Crossbreeds should have one side or the other mystically dominant, with the other being subsumed completely.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6154-deathmonkee","name":"DeathMonkee","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6154_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"58"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-29T21:16:20-07:00","id":532740,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DeathMonkee</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/529058-how-likely-would-it-be-for-a-demon-blooded-to-find-refuge-with-the-lucifuge?p=532676#post532676\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Okay, hmmmmmm.......<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> It was my understanding that a lucifuges powers, ie Castigation and the extended lifespan, came from being the child of a human and an Infernal Demon. Am I misunderstanding this?</div> </div> </div> </div> That's the fluff, the mechanics are that castigation and extended lifespan are results of having status in the lucifuge, and membership in the lucifuge isn't technically dependent on being an otherwise normal human. <br /> <br /> Slashers for example keep their endowments, I imagine one of the reasons the lucifuge kill perspective members if they don't pass muster is that they don't want to be responsible for a member turning into the thing from Jeepers Creepers. <br /> <br /> Not that I'm against such crossbred characters entirely, but I'd make it the basis of a story- A lucifuge wolf-blood who is the result of blasphemous rites between bale hounds and their demonic masters. Being the bale hound messiah probably won't be much fun for the character, hopefully the players have fun though.<br /> <br /> So I wouldn't have a demon-blooded lucifuge just because, I'd make it the result of a scheme by the God-Machine or the Lady in Milan.<br /> <br /> And as I pointed out, endowments are pretty versatile, making a lycanthropic lucifuge or demn-blooded like lucifuge etc is quite possible without giving them special advantages beyond allowing them to be creative with their custom endowments.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/391-stsword","name":"StSword","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar391_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1635"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}